{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>If I do not set, [and I will curse your blessings]</b> — like the reading of <i>yagih ḥashekhi</i> [cf. the ketiv of אגידה חשכי in the Masoretic apparatus]." "<b>And also [I will curse it]</b> — a doubled [form] in thepiel [pattern]; and the sense concerns the blessing." "<b>And also</b> — thus I have done until now, for I have cursed the blessing, because you did not take to heart."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The comparison is to Deuteronomy 31:21 or similar passages where the ketiv differs from the qeri; 'יגיה חשכי' is cryptic and rendered literally.", 1 "The reference to הכפל (doubling) likely concerns the pi'el intensity or repeated form; rendered literally without expanding."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:11.897522378Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}